# ADR-001: Use Redis for refresh token storage

## Context
JWTs are stateless. We need instant token revocation 
for logout and account suspension.

## Decision
Store refresh tokens in Redis with TTL, not in PostgreSQL.

## Consequences
+ Revocation is O(1) — just delete the Redis key
+ No DB query on every token refresh
- Adds Redis as a required infrastructure dependency
- If Redis goes down, all users are logged out